                                "target_word": "enumerated",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8fd8c50e-13fd-3193-8979-84b813945995",
                                        "entry_id": "88e5ca84-df7d-3bd9-b5ca-6df5b5b56889",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Specified (especially when fully specified) by an enumeration or list of steps, parts, values, amounts, etc.;"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3acabb33-7599-4150-a5db-f61f39fe2fd4",
                                                "sense_id": "8fd8c50e-13fd-3193-8979-84b813945995",
                                                "text": "Washington sided with Hamilton and the result was that an incidental or \"implied\" power was created that exceeded in size and scope the very enumerated power it was to implement!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c32622fd-3c9e-4704-bcef-49bc2e74f718",
                                                "sense_id": "8fd8c50e-13fd-3193-8979-84b813945995",
                                                "text": "The issue I have with H.R. 9 is I just look at it and think to myself, there are a lot of attorney's fees, and crossing T's and dotting I's, and is there going to be a little side litigation about did we fill the complaint out correctly? I mean, it just seems very enumerated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "115864a1-f34f-48e0-9a22-dd4a4fdf918b",
                                                "sense_id": "8fd8c50e-13fd-3193-8979-84b813945995",
                                                "text": "The federal government would have very narrow, very defined, very enumerated powers , while the power of states would be more expansive."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "facb3144-a2e2-3a12-a216-2ab84d4f159f",
                                        "entry_id": "88e5ca84-df7d-3bd9-b5ca-6df5b5b56889",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Specified (especially when fully specified) by an enumeration or list of steps, parts, values, amounts, etc.;",
                                            "Defined to consist of a specified list of possible values."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b7fc5e5-9e81-4edb-8df7-d204a3702854",
                                                "sense_id": "facb3144-a2e2-3a12-a216-2ab84d4f159f",
                                                "text": "Enumerated types make your code easy to modify."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e55d6ef-af6c-3d8e-b186-ac821a182edc",
                                        "entry_id": "88e5ca84-df7d-3bd9-b5ca-6df5b5b56889",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having been included or listed in an enumeration of possibilities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "068cd0b9-7dd6-4c6d-8470-23180809b118",
                                                "sense_id": "8e55d6ef-af6c-3d8e-b186-ac821a182edc",
                                                "text": "Sugar was originally an enumerated commodity which could be exported only to Great Britain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d04363f5-87f3-47fe-9142-5d55f1b3f0bb",
                                                "sense_id": "8e55d6ef-af6c-3d8e-b186-ac821a182edc",
                                                "text": "It will be seen that the scope of an enumerated motion is so wide that its determination disposes of the issues; while a nonenumerated motion, under which designation fall all motions other than those included in the enumerated class, concerns merely some matter incidental to the main course of the litigation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e4d52f3-a162-4d0d-b2b8-dcecdf213974",
                                                "sense_id": "8e55d6ef-af6c-3d8e-b186-ac821a182edc",
                                                "text": "For example, during the nineteenth century, courts often considered whether a claimed right fell within an enumerated right in the federal or state constitution."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0aed574-f9bf-4169-879a-1eaf1e95f29e",
                                                "sense_id": "8e55d6ef-af6c-3d8e-b186-ac821a182edc",
                                                "text": "As such , Congress has the very enumerated constitutional authority for requiring military service that it lacks for requiring the purchase of health insurance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cfffa22-0737-3a50-a8dc-e9b2f43aa6ca",
                                        "entry_id": "88e5ca84-df7d-3bd9-b5ca-6df5b5b56889",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having been included or listed in an enumeration of possibilities.",
                                            "Having one of the possible values specified in advance for a type defined by an enumeration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "919c85e2-a64a-4240-9629-9bbcac71d9f1",
                                                "sense_id": "4cfffa22-0737-3a50-a8dc-e9b2f43aa6ca",
                                                "text": "Continuing the analogy, just as the numeric constant Math.PI can be assigned to a variable of its type (i.e., double), an enumerated constant can be assigned to a variable of its type (e.g. Team)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63eb5b8b-9439-3215-a957-6cf5c6890141",
                                        "entry_id": "88e5ca84-df7d-3bd9-b5ca-6df5b5b56889",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having been specified by a precise numeric value."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3118540b-7739-48f4-b3ad-fddd05c2cd3e",
                                                "sense_id": "63eb5b8b-9439-3215-a957-6cf5c6890141",
                                                "text": "London, with an enumerated population of 3,814,571, showed the deaths from all causes to be 81,832, being an average of 21.5."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a2bbaf2-d1a7-4115-b5be-61257170fb39",
                                                "sense_id": "63eb5b8b-9439-3215-a957-6cf5c6890141",
                                                "text": "Certainly were the Congress through the Appropriations Committee to indicate to us that a certain enumerated amount of funds were to be made available, we would indicate to the committee how in our best judgment those funds should be distributed over the several management aspects of the total national forest system."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29f06a71-0cf8-4d8d-866e-0980f42711cf",
                                                "sense_id": "63eb5b8b-9439-3215-a957-6cf5c6890141",
                                                "text": "We said, at the time, that it was very enumerated relief . We could say very much to the dollar how much relief it would be, and that is the relief that Iran has gotten."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
